{"id":2,"word":"Spouse","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Family Members","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Very common","gujarati_pronunciation":"સ્પાઉઝ","english_meaning":"A husband or wife; a married partner.","gujarati_meaning":"પતિ અથવા પત્ની — લગ્નથી જોડાયેલ જીવનસાથી.","synonyms":["partner","husband","wife","consort"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":["legal spouse","spouse's income","surviving spouse"],"word_forms":["spouses"],"usage_note":"Gender-neutral and formal term used in legal and official contexts.","memory_tip":"'Spouse' sounds like 'house' — the person who shares your house as your partner.","examples":["Please include your spouse's name on the form.","His spouse accompanied him to the event.","She is the spouse of a well-known doctor.","The policy covers the employee and spouse."]},
{"id":3,"word":"Ancestor","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Family Members","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"એન્સેસ્ટર","english_meaning":"A person from whom one is descended; a forefather.","gujarati_meaning":"પૂર્વજ — જે વ્યક્તિઓ થી આપણો જન્મ-વંશ ચાલ્યો આવ્યો છે.","synonyms":["forefather","forebear","progenitor"],"antonyms":["descendant","offspring"],"collocations":["distant ancestor","common ancestor","ancestor worship"],"word_forms":["ancestors","ancestral"],"usage_note":"'Ancestor' refers to people further back than grandparents; grandparents can also qualify.","memory_tip":"'Ante' (before) + 'cestor' → ancestor = આપણી પહેલાં આવેલ વ્યક્તિ.","examples":["My ancestors came from a small village in Saurashtra.","She traced her ancestors back 200 years.","Our ancestors built strong communities.","He is proud of his royal ancestors."]},
{"id":4,"word":"Descendant","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Family Members","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"ડિસેન્ડન્ટ","english_meaning":"A person who is related to someone who lived in the past; offspring of a family line.","gujarati_meaning":"વંશજ — ભૂતકાળની વ્યક્તિના કુળ સાથે સંબંધ ધરાવનાર.","synonyms":["offspring","heir","progeny"],"antonyms":["ancestor","forefather"],"collocations":["direct descendant","royal descendant","descendant of immigrants"],"word_forms":["descendants"],"usage_note":"Opposite of 'ancestor'. Used in genealogy and historical contexts.","memory_tip":"'Descend' = નીચે આવવું → descendant = પેઢી-દર-પેઢી નીચે આવેલ વ્યક્તિ.","examples":["She is a direct descendant of the Maratha warriors.","The descendants of the founder run the company today.","All descendants were invited to the reunion.","He identified as a descendant of African royalty."]},
{"id":5,"word":"Guardian","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Family Members","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"ગાર્ડિયન","english_meaning":"A person who is legally responsible for the care of a child or another person.","gujarati_meaning":"વાલી — જે વ્યક્તિ કાયદેસર રીતે બાળક અથવા અન્ય વ્યક્તિ માટે જવાબદાર છે.","synonyms":["caretaker","custodian","ward"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":["legal guardian","guardian's consent","appointed guardian"],"word_forms":["guardians","guardianship"],"usage_note":"A guardian may not be a biological parent; it is a legal role.","memory_tip":"'Guard' = રક્ષા + ian → guardian = રક્ષક/વાલી.","examples":["Her uncle became her legal guardian after her parents passed away.","The school requires guardian's signature.","He was appointed as guardian of the estate.","A guardian must act in the child's best interest."]},
{"id":6,"word":"Stepparent","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Family Members","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"સ્ટેપ-પૅરન્ટ","english_meaning":"A person who is married to one's biological parent but is not one's biological parent.","gujarati_meaning":"સાવકા માતા-પિતા — જે વ્યક્તિ આપણા જૈવિક માતા-પિતા સાથે પરણ્યા છે, પણ જૈવિક નથી.","synonyms":["stepfather","stepmother"],"antonyms":["biological parent"],"collocations":["loving stepparent","stepparent role","accept a stepparent"],"word_forms":["stepparents","stepfather","stepmother"],"usage_note":"The prefix 'step-' indicates a relationship through remarriage, not by blood.","memory_tip":"'Step' = સ્ટેપ/પગથિયું → stepparent = પ્રેમ-સ્વીકારના પગલે આવેલ માતા-પિતા.","examples":["Her stepparent was very caring and kind.","He built a strong bond with his stepparent.","Accepting a stepparent can take time for children.","Her stepmother attended all her school events."]},
{"id":7,"word":"In-law","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Family Members","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Very common","gujarati_pronunciation":"ઇન-લૉ","english_meaning":"A relative by marriage, especially a parent of one's spouse.","gujarati_meaning":"સાસરિયા — લગ્ન દ્વારા મળેલ સ્વજન, ખાસ કરીને જીવનસાથીના માતા-પિતા.","synonyms":["relative by marriage","marriage relation"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":["mother-in-law","father-in-law","in-law relationship"],"word_forms":["in-laws","mother-in-law","father-in-law","brother-in-law","sister-in-law"],"usage_note":"Typically refers to spouse's parents; the plural 'in-laws' means the entire family.","memory_tip":"'In law' = કાયદા/સમાજ મુજબ → in-law = સામાજિક/કાનૂની સ્વીકૃત સ્વજન.","examples":["My in-laws are visiting next week.","She gets along well with her mother-in-law.","The in-laws hosted a grand dinner.","He respects his father-in-law deeply."]},
{"id":8,"word":"Patriarch","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Family Members","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Advanced","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"પૅટ્રિઆર્ક","english_meaning":"The male head of a family or tribe; an older, respected male leader.","gujarati_meaning":"કુળ-વડો — પરિવાર કે સમાજનો વડો (પુરુષ), જે સૌ પ્રત્યે આદર ધરાવે.","synonyms":["elder","head of family","father figure"],"antonyms":["matriarch"],"collocations":["family patriarch","tribal patriarch","respected patriarch"],"word_forms":["patriarchs","patriarchal","patriarchy"],"usage_note":"'Patriarchy' refers to a system dominated by male authority; patriarch is the individual.","memory_tip":"'Patri' = father (Latin) + 'arch' = ruler → patriarch = પિતૃ-સત્તા ધરાવનાર.","examples":["The patriarch of the family made all major decisions.","He was the respected patriarch of the village.","The patriarch blessed the newlyweds.","As the patriarch, he was responsible for everyone."]},
{"id":9,"word":"Matriarch","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Family Members","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Advanced","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"મૅટ્રિઆર્ક","english_meaning":"The female head of a family or community.","gujarati_meaning":"કુળ-વડી — પરિવાર કે સમાજની વડી (સ્ત્રી), જે સૌ ઉપર પ્રેમ-અધિકાર ધરાવે.","synonyms":["female elder","matron","head of family"],"antonyms":["patriarch"],"collocations":["family matriarch","strong matriarch","matriarch of the clan"],"word_forms":["matriarchs","matriarchal","matriarchy"],"usage_note":"In many Indian joint families, the grandmother acts as the matriarch.","memory_tip":"'Matri' = mother (Latin) + 'arch' = ruler → matriarch = માતૃ-સત્તા ધરાવનારી.","examples":["The matriarch kept the family together through hard times.","Grandmother was the matriarch of our large family.","The matriarch's word was law in the household.","She became the matriarch after her mother-in-law passed away."]},
{"id":10,"word":"Orphan","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Family Members","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"ઑર્ફન","english_meaning":"A child whose parents have died.","gujarati_meaning":"અનાથ — એ બાળક જેના માતા-પિતા બંને ગુજરી ગયા હોય.","synonyms":["parentless child","ward"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":["orphan child","orphan home","war orphan"],"word_forms":["orphans","orphaned","orphanage"],"usage_note":"'Orphaned' is the adjective form. An 'orphanage' is where orphans are cared for.","memory_tip":"'Orphan' sounds like 'orfan' — think of a child without a 'fan' (family).","examples":["The orphan was adopted by a loving family.","Many orphans live in the care home.","She volunteered at an orphanage every weekend.","The war left thousands of children orphaned."]},
{"id":11,"word":"Adopted child","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Family Members","part_of_speech":"noun phrase","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"એડોપ્ટેડ ચાઇલ્ડ","english_meaning":"A child who has been legally taken into a family as a son or daughter, though not born to them.","gujarati_meaning":"દત્તક બાળક — જે બાળકને કાયદેસર પોતાના પરિવારમાં સ્વીકારવામાં આવ્યો હોય.","synonyms":["adoptee","foster child"],"antonyms":["biological child"],"collocations":["legally adopted","adopted child rights","adopt a child"],"word_forms":["adopted children","adoption","adopt"],"usage_note":"'Adopted' is the past participle of 'adopt'. An 'adoptee' is the formal term.","memory_tip":"'Adopt' = દત્તક લેવું → adopted child = દત્તક બાળક.","examples":["Their adopted child is now a successful engineer.","The couple decided to adopt a child.","An adopted child has the same legal rights as a biological child.","She never felt different from her adopted family."]},
{"id":12,"word":"Twin","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Family Members","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"ટ્વિન","english_meaning":"One of two children born to the same mother at the same time.","gujarati_meaning":"જોડિયા — એક સાથે જ જન્મેલ બે બાળકોમાંથી એક.","synonyms":["double","co-born"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":["identical twins","fraternal twins","twin siblings"],"word_forms":["twins"],"usage_note":"Identical twins share the same DNA; fraternal twins do not.","memory_tip":"'Twin' = બે — two born together = twins!","examples":["She and her sister are identical twins.","The twins always wore matching clothes.","Fraternal twins can look very different.","He has a twin brother who lives in Canada."]},
{"id":13,"word":"Godparent","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Family Members","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"ગૉડ-પૅરન્ટ","english_meaning":"A person who sponsors a child at baptism and is responsible for their religious upbringing.","gujarati_meaning":"ધર્મ-પ્રાયોજક — ધાર્મિક વિધિ (બાપ્ટિઝમ) વખતે બાળકને આશ્રય આપનાર વ્યક્તિ.","synonyms":["sponsor","godfather","godmother"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":["chosen godparent","godparent role","ask someone to be godparent"],"word_forms":["godparents","godfather","godmother"],"usage_note":"Common in Christian families; the godparent plays a mentoring role.","memory_tip":"'God' + 'parent' → godparent = ઈશ્વર સ્વીકૃત/ધર્મ-વડીલ.","examples":["She asked her best friend to be her baby's godparent.","My godfather gave me good life advice.","The godparent attended all the child's milestones.","Being a godparent is a great responsibility."]},
{"id":14,"word":"Relative","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Family Members","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Very common","gujarati_pronunciation":"રેલેટિવ","english_meaning":"A person connected to you by blood or marriage.","gujarati_meaning":"સ્વજન/સગો — જે વ્યક્તિ સાથે લોહી અથવા લગ્ન દ્વારા સંબંધ હોય.","synonyms":["relation","kin","kinsman"],"antonyms":["stranger"],"collocations":["distant relative","close relative","visit relatives"],"word_forms":["relatives"],"usage_note":"'Relative' and 'relation' are interchangeable; 'kin' is more formal or literary.","memory_tip":"'Relate' = સંબંધ → relative = સ્વજન/સગો.","examples":["We visited relatives in Ahmedabad last summer.","She has relatives all over the world.","A distant relative left her a house in his will.","My relatives always gather for Diwali."]},
{"id":15,"word":"Nephew","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Family Members","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"નેફ્યૂ","english_meaning":"The son of one's brother or sister.","gujarati_meaning":"ભત્રીજો — ભાઈ કે બહેનનો દીકરો.","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["niece"],"collocations":["young nephew","nephew's wedding","visit my nephew"],"word_forms":["nephews"],"usage_note":"Male; for female, use 'niece'. Together, 'nibling' is a newer gender-neutral term.","memory_tip":"'Neph' sounds like 'nef' → nephew = ભત્રીજો (brother/sister's son).","examples":["My nephew just started school this year.","She bought a gift for her nephew's birthday.","His nephew looks just like him.","The nephew inherited the family business."]},
{"id":16,"word":"Niece","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Family Members","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"નીસ","english_meaning":"The daughter of one's brother or sister.","gujarati_meaning":"ભત્રીજી — ભાઈ કે બહેનની દીકરી.","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["nephew"],"collocations":["young niece","niece's graduation","favorite niece"],"word_forms":["nieces"],"usage_note":"Female counterpart of 'nephew'. Both 'niece' and 'nephew' describe the same generational relationship.","memory_tip":"'Niece' has an 'i' → niece = 'I am the daughter' (female relative).","examples":["My niece is learning to play the piano.","She is the favourite niece of the family.","His niece won first prize in the drawing competition.","The niece visited her aunt every summer."]},
{"id":17,"word":"Cousin","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Family Members","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Very common","gujarati_pronunciation":"કઝિન","english_meaning":"The child of one's uncle or aunt.","gujarati_meaning":"પિત્રાઈ/મમેરા ભાઈ-બહેન — ફોઈ, કાકા, મામા, માસીના સંતાન.","synonyms":["first cousin","relation"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":["first cousin","distant cousin","cousin marriage"],"word_forms":["cousins"],"usage_note":"In Indian culture, cousins often feel as close as siblings.","memory_tip":"'Cousin' → think 'cuz' (because) we are family — cousin = પિત્રાઈ.","examples":["I grew up with my cousins next door.","She is my first cousin on my mother's side.","We meet all our cousins at Navratri every year.","His cousin is getting married in December."]},

# ── RELATIONSHIPS & ROMANCE (18–34) ──────────────────────────────────
{"id":18,"word":"Courtship","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"કૉર્ટશિપ","english_meaning":"The period of time during which a couple develop a romantic relationship before marriage.","gujarati_meaning":"પ્રણય-સમય — લગ્ન પહેલાં પ્રેમ-સંબંધ વિકસાવવાનો ગાળો.","synonyms":["wooing","dating","romance"],"antonyms":["separation","divorce"],"collocations":["long courtship","traditional courtship","courtship rituals"],"word_forms":["courtships","court"],"usage_note":"Old-fashioned but still used; 'dating' is the modern equivalent.","memory_tip":"'Court' = રાજ-દરબારમાં પ્રભાવ — courtship = પ્રેમ જીતવાનો પ્રયાસ.","examples":["Their courtship lasted three years before marriage.","Traditional courtship involved family involvement.","He wrote letters during their courtship.","Their courtship began at a college festival."]},
{"id":19,"word":"Engagement","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Very common","gujarati_pronunciation":"એન્ગેજ્મેન્ટ","english_meaning":"A formal agreement to marry; the period between proposal and marriage.","gujarati_meaning":"સગાઈ — લગ્ન માટેની ઔપચારિક સ્વીકૃતિ અને પ્રતિજ્ઞા.","synonyms":["betrothal","promise of marriage"],"antonyms":["breakup","called off"],"collocations":["engagement ring","engagement party","announce engagement"],"word_forms":["engagements","engaged","engage"],"usage_note":"'Engaged' is the adjective ('We are engaged'). An 'engagement ring' is given at the proposal.","memory_tip":"'Engage' = જોડવું → engagement = બે જ઼િંદગી જોડવાની ઘોષણા.","examples":["They announced their engagement at a family dinner.","Her engagement ring is a beautiful diamond.","The engagement party was held at a hotel.","They had a two-year engagement before marrying."]},
{"id":20,"word":"Proposal","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"પ્રપોઝ","english_meaning":"An offer of marriage made to someone.","gujarati_meaning":"લગ્ન માટે ઔપચારિક પ્રસ્તાવ — 'શું તમે મારી સાથે લગ્ન કરશો?' એ ક્ષણ.","synonyms":["marriage offer","popping the question"],"antonyms":["rejection","breakup"],"collocations":["marriage proposal","romantic proposal","proposal accepted"],"word_forms":["proposals","propose","proposed"],"usage_note":"'Pop the question' is an informal expression for making a proposal.","memory_tip":"'Propose' = આગળ મૂકવું → proposal = લગ્ન માટે આગ્રહ.","examples":["He made a romantic proposal on the rooftop.","She accepted his proposal with tears of joy.","The proposal surprised everyone in the family.","He planned the proposal for months."]},
{"id":21,"word":"Betrothed","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"adjective / noun","difficulty":"Advanced","frequency":"Less common","gujarati_pronunciation":"બિટ્રૉધ્ડ","english_meaning":"Formally engaged to be married; one's fiancé or fiancée.","gujarati_meaning":"સગાઈ-બદ્ધ — જેની સાથે સગાઈ થઈ ચૂકી છે; મંગેતર.","synonyms":["fiancé","fiancée","engaged","pledged"],"antonyms":["single","unattached"],"collocations":["betrothed couple","his betrothed","officially betrothed"],"word_forms":["betroth","betrothal"],"usage_note":"Formal/literary term; in everyday speech 'fiancé/fiancée' is used.","memory_tip":"'Be-troth' → 'troth' = pledge (જૂની અંગ્રેજીમાં) → betrothed = પ્રતિજ્ઞા-બદ્ધ.","examples":["The betrothed couple met every evening in the garden.","She was betrothed at a young age.","His betrothed came from a noble family.","The betrothal ceremony was grand and traditional."]},
{"id":22,"word":"Fiancé","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"ફ઼િઓન્સે","english_meaning":"A man who is engaged to be married.","gujarati_meaning":"મંગેતર (પુરુષ) — જે પુરુષ સાથે સગાઈ થઈ હોય.","synonyms":["betrothed","intended","partner"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":["meet my fiancé","fiancé's family","introduce fiancé"],"word_forms":["fiancés","fiancée (female)"],"usage_note":"'Fiancé' (one 'e') = male; 'fiancée' (two 'e's) = female. Both from French.","memory_tip":"Fi-ahn-SAY: fiancé = engagement (male). Think 'say yes' = engaged!","examples":["She introduced her fiancé to her parents last night.","Her fiancé proposed at the beach.","My fiancé and I are planning a December wedding.","Her fiancé is kind and caring."]},
{"id":23,"word":"Fiancée","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"ફ઼િઓન્સે","english_meaning":"A woman who is engaged to be married.","gujarati_meaning":"મંગેતર (સ્ત્રી) — જે સ્ત્રી સાથે સગાઈ થઈ હોય.","synonyms":["betrothed","intended","partner"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":["my fiancée","fiancée's wishes","fiancée's family"],"word_forms":["fiancées"],"usage_note":"'Fiancée' = female; 'fiancé' = male. Both pronounced the same way.","memory_tip":"'Fiancée' has two e's — like two people in love, the extra 'e' is for the woman.","examples":["He introduced his fiancée at the party.","His fiancée chose a simple wedding dress.","They met his fiancée's parents last week.","His fiancée works as a teacher."]},
{"id":24,"word":"Matrimony","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Advanced","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"મૅટ્રિમોની","english_meaning":"The state of being married; the formal institution of marriage.","gujarati_meaning":"વૈવાહિક જીવન — લગ્ન-સંસ્થાની ઔપચારિક અવસ્થા.","synonyms":["marriage","wedlock","union"],"antonyms":["divorce","separation","celibacy"],"collocations":["holy matrimony","enter matrimony","bonds of matrimony"],"word_forms":["matrimonial"],"usage_note":"More formal and religious than 'marriage'. Often used in ceremonies.","memory_tip":"'Matri' = mother (Latin) → matrimony = ઘર-સ્થાપના/ગૃહિણીનું ક્ષેત્ર.","examples":["They were joined in holy matrimony.","Matrimony is considered sacred in many cultures.","The couple entered into matrimony after a long courtship.","A matrimonial site helped them find each other."]},
{"id":25,"word":"Reconciliation","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Advanced","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"રિકૉન્સિલિએશન","english_meaning":"The process of making two people or groups friendly again after a disagreement.","gujarati_meaning":"સમાધાન — ઝઘડા કે ભૂલ પછી ફરીથી મૈત્રી/સ્નેહ સ્થાપવાની પ્રક્રિયા.","synonyms":["resolution","settlement","reunion","making up"],"antonyms":["estrangement","conflict","rift"],"collocations":["seek reconciliation","marital reconciliation","path to reconciliation"],"word_forms":["reconcile","reconciled","reconciliatory"],"usage_note":"Often used in both romantic and political contexts.","memory_tip":"'Re' (again) + 'concile' (council/harmony) → reconciliation = ફરી સ્નેહ-મિલન.","examples":["After months apart, their reconciliation was emotional.","Couples therapy helped their reconciliation.","The family reunion led to reconciliation among siblings.","He made the first step toward reconciliation."]},
{"id":26,"word":"Affection","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Very common","gujarati_pronunciation":"અફ઼ૅક્શન","english_meaning":"A gentle feeling of fondness or liking for someone.","gujarati_meaning":"પ્રેમ-ભાવ/સ્નેહ — કોઈ પ્રત્યે હળવો, ઊષ્મ-ભરી લાગણી.","synonyms":["fondness","love","warmth","tenderness"],"antonyms":["coldness","indifference","hatred"],"collocations":["show affection","deep affection","terms of affection"],"word_forms":["affectionate","affectionately"],"usage_note":"'Affectionate' is the adjective; 'affection' is milder than 'love'.","memory_tip":"'Affect' = અસર → affection = હૃદય પર અસર = સ્નેહ.","examples":["She showed great affection toward her grandchildren.","He greeted his old friend with genuine affection.","Children need affection and attention to thrive.","Their affection for each other was obvious."]},
{"id":27,"word":"Devotion","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"ડિવોશન","english_meaning":"Strong love, loyalty, or commitment to a person or cause.","gujarati_meaning":"ભક્તિ/સમર્પણ — ઊંડો પ્રેમ, વફ઼ાદારી; સ્વ-ભૂલીને અન્ય માટે જીવવું.","synonyms":["dedication","loyalty","commitment","love"],"antonyms":["neglect","disloyalty","indifference"],"collocations":["show devotion","devotion to family","lifelong devotion"],"word_forms":["devoted","devote","devotedly"],"usage_note":"Used for both religious and personal relationships.","memory_tip":"'Devote' = સમર્પિત → devotion = ચૂટ-ભૂટ ભૂલ્યા વગ઼ર ચોટ્ટ ચઢ઼ેલ ભાવ.","examples":["Her devotion to her family is admirable.","He showed his devotion by being there every day.","Their marriage was built on love and devotion.","Religious devotion brought the couple closer."]},
{"id":28,"word":"Infatuation","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Advanced","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"ઇન્ફ઼ૅચ્યૂએશન","english_meaning":"An intense but short-lived passion or admiration for someone.","gujarati_meaning":"ઘેલ — કોઈ પ્રત્યે તીવ્ર પણ ટૂંકા ગળ઼ ના ઉત્સાહ-ભરી પ્રેમ-ભ્રમ.","synonyms":["crush","obsession","puppy love","infatuation"],"antonyms":["indifference","hatred"],"collocations":["teenage infatuation","mere infatuation","infatuation fades"],"word_forms":["infatuate","infatuated"],"usage_note":"Distinct from true love; infatuation is intense but temporary.","memory_tip":"'Infat' sounds like 'infant' — infatuation = baby-love, not deep mature love.","examples":["His infatuation with her faded after a few months.","She mistook infatuation for love.","Infatuation is common in teenage years.","What started as infatuation turned into lasting love."]},
{"id":29,"word":"Compatibility","category":"Family & Relationships","subcategory":"Relationships & Romance","part_of_speech":"noun","difficulty":"Intermediate","frequency":"Common","gujarati_pronunciation":"કૉમ્પૅટિબિલિટી","english_meaning":"The ability of two people to exist and work together harmoniously.","gujarati_meaning":"અનુકૂળતા — બે વ્યક્તિઓ વચ્ચે સ્વભાવ-મૂલ્ય-જીવન-શૈલી ની સુસંગતતા.","synonyms":["harmony","agreement","suitability"],"antonyms":["incompatibility","mismatch"],"collocations":["relationship compatibility","test compatibility","compatibility issues"],"word_forms":["compatible","incompatible","compatibly"],"usage_note":"Used in both romantic and professional contexts.","memory_tip":"'Compat' (together) + 'ibility' → compatibility = સાથે ટળ-ઓ-ટળ ચાલી શકવાની ક્ષ઼મતા.","examples":["They checked their compatibility before marriage.","Compatibility is key to a happy marriage.","The couple had great emotional compatibility.","Astrology is often used to check compatibility in India."]},
